 "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Gupta RK", "lastName": "Gupta", "firstName": "Rishi K", "initials": "RK", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6257-1285"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Institute for Global Health, University College London, London, UK."}, {"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Marks M", "lastName": "Marks", "firstName": "Michael", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7585-4743"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}, {"affiliation": "Clinical Research Dept, Faculty of Infectious and Tropical Diseases, London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Samuels THA", "lastName": "Samuels", "firstName": "Thomas H A", "initials": "THA", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6177-2165"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Luintel A", "lastName": "Luintel", "firstName": "Akish", "initials": "A", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Rampling T", "lastName": "Rampling", "firstName": "Tommy", "initials": "T", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9111-2486"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Chowdhury H", "lastName": "Chowdhury", "firstName": "Humayra", "initials": "H", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Quartagno M", "lastName": "Quartagno", "firstName": "Matteo", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4446-0730"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "MRC Clinical Trials Unit, Institute of Clinical Trials and Methodology, University College London, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Nair A", "lastName": "Nair", "firstName": "Arjun", "initials": "A", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9270-3771"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lipman M", "lastName": "Lipman", "firstName": "Marc", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7501-4448"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "UCL Respiratory, Division of Medicine, University College London, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Abubakar I", "lastName": "Abubakar", "firstName": "Ibrahim", "initials": "I", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0370-1430"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Institute for Global Health, University College London, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "van Smeden M", "lastName": "van Smeden", "firstName": "Maarten", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5529-1541"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Julius Center for Health Sciences and Primary Care, University Medical Center Utrecht, Utrecht University, Utrecht, The Netherlands."}]}}, {"fullName": "Wong WK", "lastName": "Wong", "firstName": "Wai Keong", "initials": "WK", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Williams B", "lastName": "Williams", "firstName": "Bryan", "initials": "B", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8094-1841"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "NIHR University College London Hospitals Biomedical Research Centre, London, UK."}, {"affiliation": "University College London, London, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Noursadeghi M", "lastName": "Noursadeghi", "firstName": "Mahdad", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4774-0853"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University College London Hospitals NHS Trust, London, UK."}, {"affiliation": "Division of Infection and Immunity, University College London, London, UK."}]}}, {"collectiveName": "UCLH COVID-19 Reporting Group"}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7389-1527"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7501-4448"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9111-2486"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-9270-3771"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0370-1430"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4774-0853"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5529-1541"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6177-2165"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6257-1285"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7585-4743"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8094-1841"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2415-4824"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3113-1188"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4446-0730"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0009-2766-3158"}]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "6", "volume": "56", "journalIssueId": 3065737, "dateOfPublication": "2020 Dec", "monthOfPublication": 12, "yearOfPublication": 2020, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Eur Respir J", "title": "The European respiratory journal", "essn": "1399-3003", "issn": "0903-1936", "isoabbreviation": "Eur Respir J", "nlmid": "8803460"}, "printPublicationDate": "2020-12-01"}, "pubYear": "2020", "pageInfo": "2003498", "abstractText": "The number of proposed prognostic models for coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) is growing rapidly, but it is unknown whether any are suitable for widespread clinical implementation.We independently externally validated the performance of candidate prognostic models, identified through a living systematic review, among consecutive adults admitted to hospital with a final diagnosis of COVID-19. We reconstructed candidate models as per original descriptions and evaluated performance for their original intended outcomes using predictors measured at the time of admission. We assessed discrimination, calibration and net benefit, compared to the default strategies of treating all and no patients, and against the most discriminating predictors in univariable analyses.We tested 22 candidate prognostic models among 411 participants with COVID-19, of whom 180 (43.8%) and 115 (28.0%) met the endpoints of clinical deterioration and mortality, respectively. Highest areas under receiver operating characteristic (AUROC) curves were achieved by the NEWS2 score for prediction of deterioration over 24 h (0.78, 95% CI 0.73-0.83), and a novel model for prediction of deterioration <14 days from admission (0.78, 95% CI 0.74-0.82). The most discriminating univariable predictors were admission oxygen saturation on room air for in-hospital deterioration (AUROC 0.76, 95% CI 0.71-0.81), and age for in-hospital mortality (AUROC 0.76, 95% CI 0.71-0.81). No prognostic model demonstrated consistently higher net benefit than these univariable predictors, across a range of threshold probabilities.Admission oxygen saturation on room air and patient age are strong predictors of deterioration and mortality among hospitalised adults with COVID-19, respectively. None of the prognostic models evaluated here offered incremental value for patient stratification to these univariable predictors.", "affiliation": "Institute for Global Health, University College London, London, UK.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic-Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Validation Study", "Journal Article", "Observational Study"]}, "grantsList": {"gra